---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Bespoke web applications"
  description="Focused web applications built around your people and processes, connected to the business systems you already use."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="Bespoke applications"
    title="Give your workflow a place to work."
    description="Bring the work around your ERP into a focused web application. Built for the people doing the task, with the information they need in reach."
  />
  <section class="section service-area">
    <div class="wrap editorial-split">
      <h2>
        Start with the
        <br />
        missing step.
      </h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Some processes end up spread across spreadsheets, emails and business
          software. People become the connection: copying records, checking
          statuses and passing decisions from one system to another.
        </p>
        <p>
          A bespoke application gives that work a clear path. We map the
          process, identify what belongs in your existing systems, and build the
          interface and functionality that complete it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/solutions/quality-control/">
            See a connected QC workflow <Icon />
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section studio-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>
          A focused scope.
          <br />
          Room to develop.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Get the useful first workflow working, then build on what you learn.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-list">
        <article class="service">
          <h3>Understand the work.</h3>
          <p>
            Walk through the process, exceptions and handoffs with the people
            using it. Agree what a successful first version needs to do.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="service">
          <h3>Build and connect.</h3>
          <p>
            Shape the interface around the task and connect it to the records
            and operations in your existing systems.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="service">
          <h3>Put it to work.</h3>
          <p>
            Test the real workflow together. Agree deployment, support and the
            next improvements around practical use.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
